_ ¶ long-section
    - number Int

## Section ${number}: measuring the transcript

Every section in this document has the same shape, so the page ends up hundreds of blocks long. It shows how a long reply scrolls and how long it takes to lay out before the transcript is virtualized.

- The first point of section ${number}, with **bold** and `code`
- The second point, long enough to wrap onto another line when the column is narrow or the source pane is open
- The third point

```yumi
. section = ${number}
. blocks = markdown-blocks(source)
```

| Run | Blocks | Laid out | Painted |
| :-- | --: | --: | --: |
| ${number}a | 120 | 4.1 ms | 2.0 ms |
| ${number}b | 480 | 15.8 ms | 2.2 ms |

> Section ${number} ends here.

