_ ¶ inline-source

Plain text with **bold**, *italic*, and `inline code` in one sentence.

Emphasis can use underscores too: _italic_ and __bold__. Styles nest: **bold with *italic* inside**, *italic with **bold** inside*, and ***both at once***.

Styles can touch punctuation (**bold**, *italic*; `code`.) and sit inside a word: un**believ**able. Names like snake_case_identifier stay literal, and 2 * 3 * 4 is arithmetic, not emphasis.

Links come in several shapes: [a plain link](https://example.com), [a **bold** link](https://example.com/bold), [a link with `code`](https://example.com/code), and **[a link inside bold](https://example.com/inside)**.

Images have no pixels to show yet, so they fall back to their label: ![A diagram of the layout tree](https://example.com/tree.png)

Inline code keeps its contents literal: `**not bold**`, `[not](a-link)`, and `a < b && b > c`.

Escapes keep markers literal: \\*not italic\\*, \\`not code\\`, and \\[not a link\\](nowhere).

Inline code wraps like text when a sentence carries a lot of it: `transcript.scroll-to-end(Orientation.vertical)` then `window.markup-batch-queue.checkpoint()` then `session.append-reply(text)` and finally `session.finish-reply()`.

**A whole paragraph can be bold, and when it is long enough it has to wrap across several lines while keeping its weight on every one of them.**

*A whole paragraph can be italic too, and it should keep its slant on every line when it wraps past the edge of the column.*

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ¶ paragraphs-source

A short paragraph.

A long paragraph should wrap cleanly at the edge of the column and keep an even rhythm from line to line. It has enough sentences to fill several lines at any reasonable width, which makes it easy to see whether the line spacing is comfortable, whether the right edge is ragged in a pleasant way, and whether the gap before the next paragraph is clearly larger than the gap between lines.

This paragraph is written
across several source lines
that are joined by soft breaks,
so it should read as one flowing sentence.

One.

Two.

Three short paragraphs in a row show the paragraph gap on its own.

A paragraph with a very long word, Pneumonoultramicroscopicsilicovolcanoconiosis, in the middle of ordinary text.

A long address with nowhere to break: https://example.com/a/very/long/path/that/keeps/going/and/going/without/any/spaces/to/break/on/until/it/passes/the/column/width?with=query&and=parameters

