     1. Natural tracks
     2. Shrinking tracks
3. Ship

- A parent item whose text is long enough to wrap onto a second line, so the hanging indent at the outer level is visible.
  - A nested item whose text is also long enough to wrap, which checks that the hanging indent follows the nesting depth and does not fall back to the outer margin.
    - A third level that wraps as well, because deep items have the least room and are the most likely to break in an ugly place.
- Back at the outer level.

