_ ¶ grid-pressure-source

Cells with a lot of text share the width and wrap:

| Layout | When to use it | Trade-off |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Flex | Children sit along one axis and share the leftover space by weight. | It knows nothing about the other rows, so columns in separate rows never line up. |
| Flow | Children wrap onto new lines when a line fills up, like words in a paragraph. | Line breaks depend on content, so the shape changes as text changes. |
| Grid | Children fall into shared columns that are sized from the widest cell in each one. | Every cell has to be measured before any column width is known. |

More columns than fit, so the table scrolls sideways:

| Region | Mon | Tue | Wed | Thu | Fri | Sat | Sun | Week | Month | Quarter | Year |
| :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |
| North America | 1,204 | 1,310 | 980 | 1,422 | 1,515 | 640 | 512 | 7,583 | 31,090 | 94,417 | 381,204 |
| Europe | 1,020 | 1,115 | 1,090 | 1,204 | 1,310 | 590 | 470 | 6,799 | 28,410 | 86,003 | 351,760 |
| Asia Pacific | 1,190 | 1,288 | 1,004 | 1,391 | 1,560 | 702 | 498 | 7,633 | 30,774 | 93,002 | 377,960 |

A narrow label column beside one very long cell:

| Flag | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `-o` | Write the compiled program to the given path instead of running it, creating any missing directories on the way and replacing whatever file is already there. |
| `-q` | Stay quiet. |

Many rows:

| Step | Task | Owner | Status |
| ---: | --- | --- | :-: |
| 1 | Parse alignment colons | parser | done |
| 2 | Carry alignment on the table node | parser | done |
| 3 | Measure natural column widths | layout | done |
| 4 | Shrink the widest columns first | layout | done |
| 5 | Keep a floor under each column | layout | done |
| 6 | Measure rows at the final widths | layout | done |
| 7 | Stretch cells to their row | layout | done |
| 8 | Scroll when floors overflow | chat | done |
| 9 | Style the header row | chat | done |
| 10 | Draw rules between rows | chat | done |
| 11 | Virtualize long transcripts | chat | next |
